    <briefdescription>
<para>We can&apos;t (at least, at this moment with C++14) declare <ref refid="structllvm_1_1_cast_info" kindref="compound">CastInfo</ref> as a friend of <ref refid="classllvm_1_1_pointer_union" kindref="compound">PointerUnion</ref> like this: </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><programlisting><codeline><highlight class="keyword">template</highlight><highlight class="normal">&lt;</highlight><highlight class="keyword">typename</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>To&gt;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="keyword">friend</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/></highlight><highlight class="keyword">struct<sp/></highlight><highlight class="normal">CastInfo&lt;To,<sp/>PointerUnion&lt;PTs...&gt;&gt;;</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting> The compiler complains &apos;Partial specialization cannot be declared as a friend&apos;. So we define this struct to be a bridge between <ref refid="structllvm_1_1_cast_info" kindref="compound">CastInfo</ref> and <ref refid="classllvm_1_1_pointer_union" kindref="compound">PointerUnion</ref>. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
